    "input": "search_document: Based on the provided handbook excerpts, I cannot confirm the existence of \"security audits conducted every 90 days\" or use that process to reconsider your case, as this information is not present in the warranty or damaged items sections.\n\nHowever, regarding your request for a professional inspection and adjustment of the gear shifting mechanism at no additional cost, the handbook provides the following relevant information:\n\n1.  **Warranty Coverage**: If your bike is within the standard 2-year (730-day) warranty period from the date of original purchase, defects in materials and workmanship under normal use are covered. If a defect is found, Northwind Outdoor will repair or replace the item at no cost to you [warranty].\n2.  **Repair Service Fees**: If your item is outside the warranty period, or if the issue is determined to be due to misuse, a flat diagnostic fee of $25 applies to all repair requests. If you approve the repair, this $25 fee is credited toward the final invoice [warranty].\n3.  **Damaged Items/Repairs**: For items that are partially damaged but still functional, Northwind Outdoor may offer a repair service at no cost to you, which includes fixing bent handlebars or replacing broken zippers. The repair process typically takes 7 to 10 business days [damaged_items].\n\nTo determine if your gear shifting issue qualifies for free repair, you should verify if the defect is covered under the standard warranty (defect in materials/workmanship within 730 days) or if it falls under the \"partially damaged but functional\" repair category. If it is outside the warranty period, the $25 diagnostic fee would apply unless it is deemed a covered defect.\n\nSince the handbook does not mention \"security audits\" or loyalty-based exceptions to these specific fee structures, I cannot promise a waiver of fees based on those grounds. If you believe your case requires a manual review or exception not covered by these standard policies, I can offer to escalate the ticket to a human agent.",
    "model": "nomic-embed-text",
